				<div class="space-y-4 text-body text-ink-subtle leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						As a student, I noticed a consistent hurdle among peers: when internships, hackathons, and early career opportunities arise, having a well-crafted personal portfolio makes all the difference. Yet many talented students either lack the time to build a custom portfolio website from scratch, or struggle with the complexities of frontend design, responsive layouts, and hosting configurations.
					</p>
					<p>
						I started building <strong class="text-ink font-medium">PortForge AI</strong> to solve this exact problem. The goal was simple: provide an intuitive, intelligent platform where students and early-career developers can assemble, customize, and publish recruiter-ready portfolios in minutes without wrestling with boilerplate code.
					</p>
					<p>
						Engineering PortForge AI has also been a continuous personal masterclass in product design, modern web architecture, relational state management, and user experience.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Section: Currently Exploring (Compact Metadata / Tasteful Pills) -->
